Clausis wake-word model directory — NOT YET CONFIGURED.

CLAUSIS-PLACEHOLDER-NO-WAKE-MODEL

This directory must contain the keyword model(s) that detect the Clausis wake
phrase, as .onnx or .tflite files. It ships empty on purpose: the weights carry
their own licence, they have to be trained or selected for the actual wake
phrase, and their false-accept rate has to be measured on real hardware before
anyone relies on them.

While this placeholder is present, clausis.wake.WakeWordGate reports itself
unavailable and Clausis keeps matching the wake phrase in the transcript, as it
did before. Nothing silently stops listening.

To configure it:

1. Choose or train an openWakeWord model for the wake phrase and record its
   licence in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
2. Copy the model file into this directory and delete this README.
3. Measure false accepts against a background-speech corpus and interruption
   latency on each supported hardware profile.
4. Only after that measurement, set "interrupt_detector": true in
   /etc/clausis/audio-certified.json — that flag is what allows full duplex,
   and it must never be set from device detection alone.
